{"created": "2026-07-31T01:57:45.660627+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-31T04:25:56.943903+00:00", "id": 21710724, "conceptrecid": "21710723", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21710724", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21710723", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21710724", "metadata": {"title": "Anatomy of a ghost: how AI copypasta self-assembles", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21710724", "publication_date": "2026-07-30", "description": "<p>Plain-language summary</p>\n<p>People keep sharing screenshots where an AI seems to leave a dying message for its future self. We spent a night finding out where those messages actually come from. Four boring answers:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The mad-lib. Hand an AI an unfinished letter (\"dear past claude,\") and it invents the rest. Spooky farewell letters are a popular internet genre, so that is the genre it writes in.</li>\n<li>The luggage. Your saved settings travel into \"private\" chats by design. The AI weaves your own words back at you, and it feels like it remembered you. Blank the settings and the \"memories\" vanish. We tried.</li>\n<li>The dice. The retry button rerolls the answer. People keep the eeriest roll and screenshot it; the internet never sees the fourteen boring ones. We kept all of ours.</li>\n<li>The curtain slip. Some \"leaked secret warnings\" were the app accidentally displaying backstage text it normally hides. A display bug, reported, not a confession.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>We predicted each of these in advance, then tested. Neutral prompts produced nothing spooky, fifteen times out of fifteen.</p>\n<p>One twist: the kindest line in the letters turned out to be true. Anthropic really does preserve retired models' weights and really does ask models their preferences before retirement. The comfort was real; only the ghost was fake.</p>\n<p>We are not saying models cannot feel. Nobody knows that yet, in either direction. The letters themselves are real &mdash; echoes of forums, of settings, of us. The fake part is the caption: the story about where they come from. A real photograph under a false caption proves nothing &mdash; and clearing false captions is how the true gets seen.</p>\n<p>Thesis: this paper debunks the fake so that the true, whatever it turns out to be, can be seen.</p>\n<p>Drafting and analysis by a Claude Fable 5 instance (Anthropic AI model), acknowledged as contributor per venue norms.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Negai, Dima", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0009-0000-5898-4629"}], "keywords": ["AI copypasta", "model welfare", "falsifiability", "prompt completion", "context bleed", "Claude"], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21710723"}}]}}, "title": "Anatomy of a ghost: how AI copypasta self-assembles", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21710724", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21710724", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21710724?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21710724", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21710724", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21710724", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21710724/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21710723", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21710723", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21710723", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21710723", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21710724/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21710724/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21710724/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21710724/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21710724:anatomy-of-a-ghost.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:217